/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:14340:      "docstring": "Grow four clockwise spiral wall paths from the tips of a teal cross.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = 0 (black). A single teal (8) cross centered in the grid.\n\nRule:\n- Each arm tip launches a \"turtle\" heading 90° right of its outward direction.\n- Movement priority: turn right > go straight > turn left (left only if not on border).\n- Normal step = 2 cells; step right after a turn = 1 cell.\n- Each new cell must have a 1-cell orthogonal gap from all existing walls except the predecessor.\n\nKey insight: The right-turn preference plus alternating 2/1 step lengths creates self-avoiding spirals that tile the grid with uniform spacing.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:14348:        "path": "each endpoint emits ray clockwise spiraling inward/outward, turning 90 degrees at boundaries or when spacing constraint requires, with initial backward step before proceeding",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:14356:          "ray casting",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:14366:        "catalog:ray_casting",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:14372:        "code:ray_loop",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:14377:        "operation:ray_cast",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:14392:        "alternating",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:14475:        "ray",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:14518:        "code:ray_loop"
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:14525:      "docstring": "Expand a 3x3 block motif into a 5x5 block motif around its missing center.\n\nInput structure:\n- Teal background surrounds one 9x9 foreground motif.\n- The motif is a 3x3 array of 3x3 blocks; the middle block is empty teal.\n- Colored pixels immediately around the empty middle block encode the border\n  of the missing center block.\n\nRule:\n- Keep the original 9x9 motif in place.\n- Copy each of the eight surrounding 3x3 blocks to the opposite outer slot\n  of the implied 5x5 block grid, without rotating it.\n- Fill the center block from the eight pixels around the hole; its center is\n  the motif's majority foreground color.\n\nKey insight: The visible 9x9 motif is the middle of a larger periodic\nblock-level pattern, and the empty center is reconstructed from its immediate\ninner boundary.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:14529:        "src": "the visible 9x9 motif: a 3x3 array of 3x3 blocks with the center block missing",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:14539:        "code:ray_loop",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:14545:        "operation:ray_cast",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:14558:        "array",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:14636:        "code:ray_loop",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:14644:      "docstring": "Connect same-color diagonal pixel pairs, then emit perpendicular rays from differently-colored pixels on those diagonals.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color. Line color (e.g. blue) has pixel pairs aligned on shared diagonals. Trigger color (e.g. magenta) pixels sit along those diagonals.\n\nRule:\n- Draw diagonal lines connecting each pair of same-color aligned pixels.\n- Where the diagonal crosses a trigger pixel, emit perpendicular diagonal rays (in the trigger's color) extending to the grid boundary.\n\nKey insight: Trigger pixels act as beam-splitters — the perpendicular rays rotate 90° from the connecting diagonal's orientation.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:14659:          "ray-cast",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:14673:        "catalog:diagonal_ray",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:14678:        "code:ray_loop",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:14683:        "operation:ray_cast",
