/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:40352:      "docstring": "Recolor the unique safe route between the two maroon endpoints from teal to maroon.\n\nInput structure\n- A black background contains a teal 4-connected track, exactly two maroon endpoint pixels, and one or more orange blocker pixels embedded near the track.\n\nRule\n- Treat each orange blocker and its 8-neighborhood as forbidden.\n- In the remaining teal/maroon track graph, there is exactly one simple\n  4-connected path between the maroon endpoints.\n- Recolor teal pixels on that path to maroon; leave endpoints, blockers, and all other cells unchanged.\n\nKey insight\n- The orange pixels block nearby teal cells diagonally as well as orthogonally, which removes shorter decoy routes and makes the intended endpoint-to-endpoint path unique.",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:40357:        "path": "unique shortest 4-connected route between the endpoints through teal/maroon cells after treating every orange blocker and its 8-neighborhood as forbidden",
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/skill/arc-codegen-similar-local/arc_reference_index.json:40359:        "transform": "keep the endpoints, orange blockers, black background, and off-route teal cells unchanged"
