/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/4/code.py:25:#   sprites" in isolation, but "ray crosses a sprite, that sprite is erased, and the same beam
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/4/code.py:27:# - Small trace: suppose two left-facing copies share the same rows, with a blocker at col 6..7
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/4/code.py:29:#   scan at the blocker and never discovers the marker. D5-only logic finds the marker and paints
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/4/code.py:30:#   through bg gaps while leaving the blocker intact. The fused logic finds the marker, marks row 3
