/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/4/code.py:45:# - `_first_marker_on_ray(...)` used to treat "first non-bg" as decisive. That fails because a
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/4/code.py:46:#   blocker sprite may appear before the marker. The fused version must scan to the boundary and
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/4/code.py:49:#   stop rays, and hit sprites must be removed instead of preserved.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/4/code.py:52:#   then replay the ray paths so the beam can occupy the destroyed lanes.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/4/code.py:59:#   active edge, with a left-side blocker between them. This guarantees true D5-style occluded
